                                "sense_id": "59cee969-ea22-35f0-8b98-695be616d7f3",
                                "text": "All this time France was substantially as tranquil as England herself, and decidedly more prosperous, though annoyed and impeded by the incessant plottings of traitors in her councils and other exalted stations to resubject her to kingly sway."
